<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28374" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdŭli</span></b> ,
		ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in Aquitanian Gaul, whose coast
				was famous for its oysters</i>, in the mod. <i>Medoc</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 2</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">7, 1</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdŭlus</span></b> 
			or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdŭ-lĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to the Meduli, Medulian</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 6,
				21, § 62</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdŭlĭcus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Medulian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">supellex,</span>”
				i. e. <i>oysters</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 8, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
